WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.735
♪ -Do not read, do not read ♪

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.537
♪ Do not read these books,
these books ♪

00:00:05.537 --> 00:00:07.173
-Now, before we start,

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.874
I just want you all to know
that every book

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:11.644
that I'm about to show you
is 100% real.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.246
These are actual books.
You can find them on Amazon

00:00:14.246 --> 00:00:17.216
or check them out at your local
library. They are real.

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:19.686
Alright. Let's see what's on
my "do not read" list.

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:22.622
This first one is just --
This just gets the party going.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.391
This is fantastic.

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:28.261
I can't even believe I'm holding
it and not reading it.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.029
It is a reference book.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:33.966
It is called "Land Snails
and Slugs of Russia

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.201
and Adjacent Countries."

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.169
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.338
It's a classic page turner.

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.905
I'm just going to --
I'm just going to go home

00:00:39.905 --> 00:00:41.507
and just read
the whole thing tonight.

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:43.242
And if you want to know

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:45.544
what life is like
studying snails and slugs,

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:46.679
if you want to see
what it does to a person,

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.013
there you go. Look at this guy.

00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:49.382
"Hey."
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:53.586
[ Russian accent ] "Hey, am I
too early for the party?

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.554
What are you guys
talking about?

00:00:55.554 --> 00:00:58.224
Slugs? Oh, you were not?

00:00:58.224 --> 00:01:00.526
Oh, you should be.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.228
Great party either way.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.731
I came early.

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:08.835
I brought the dog
and some slugs."

00:01:08.835 --> 00:01:10.269
[ Normal voice ] Let's check out
this next one.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:12.404
This is a how-to book.

00:01:12.404 --> 00:01:16.809
This is "50 Nifty Ways
to Jazz Up Your Jeans."

00:01:16.809 --> 00:01:19.245
I'm all about jazzing up
my jeans, man.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:21.681
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:24.683
This is perfect
for the pandemic, I think.

00:01:24.683 --> 00:01:26.485
Let's see what's in here.

00:01:26.485 --> 00:01:29.622
Oh, yeah, I like this one here.
This one's called party pants.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:30.856
See, look at this one here.

00:01:30.856 --> 00:01:32.825
It's very simple.
You just glue

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:35.094
a tic-tac-toe board
on your jeans.

00:01:35.094 --> 00:01:36.930
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.732
Then you ask everyone to just
draw on your nether regions.

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.035
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:44.170
Oh, actually it says --
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.573
It says, "Note --

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:48.541
You should not wear your jeans
because the glue

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:50.142
could seep through
and you could be stuck

00:01:50.142 --> 00:01:51.644
wearing your party pants
for a long time."

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.713
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:54.714
-Now you tell me.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:56.349
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.850
-How long you've been
wearing your party pants?

00:01:57.850 --> 00:02:01.187
-Dude, too long.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.556
This next up is
a children's book.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.825
I love kids books, obviously.
You know that, man.

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.627
This one's called

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.828
"What's Growing
in Grandma's Garden?"

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:11.364
And then if you zoom in,
it says,

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:13.299
"a book to help grown-ups
have a conversation

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:14.968
with children about cannabis."

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:19.038
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.572
-Wait, what?

00:02:20.572 --> 00:02:21.707
-Never too early
to teach your kids

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:25.178
about how grandma
loves to get baked.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:27.246
There you go.
Let's take a look inside.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.648
You got some people
there eating,

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:30.849
kids playing under a tree.

00:02:30.849 --> 00:02:34.020
And then there's grandma
just chilling by herself

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.421
in front of...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:36.822
-That's Grandma?

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:39.525
-...a locked greenhouse.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:41.127
-She's like Martha Stewart.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:44.297
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.765
What's growing in -- Alright.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.500
This next one here

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.269
is an activity book
for the whole family.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:52.504
It is called

00:02:52.504 --> 00:02:56.142
"Family Fun in Tape Recording."

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:57.877
It says here,
"great new all-purpose book

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:01.447
for everyone who owns or dreams
of owning a tape recorder."

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:02.581
[ Laughter ]

00:03:02.581 --> 00:03:03.950
Well, let's see what kind of fun
we can have

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.418
with the tape recorder.

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.486
Ooh, here's one.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.055
It's called "whistle
while you tape."

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:12.492
Find out from your guests how
many can whistle loud and clear.

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:15.495
Let them prove it by taping
their whistling prowess,

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.963
then divide them into teams.

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:22.435
Next, hand each contestant
a dry salted soda cracker.

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:24.470
God. That's fun.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:26.472
[ Laughter ]
-I used to do that.

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:28.874
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.843
Got my first tape recorder
in '79.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:33.246
Used to do stuff like that.

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.615
-Did you pass out crackers?

00:03:35.615 --> 00:03:38.017
-No, I didn't.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:42.488
Soda cracker is basically the
party pants of tape-recording.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.022
-I got it. I got the memo.

00:03:44.022 --> 00:03:46.926
-Jazz up your jeans, man.

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.861
This next book here
is a cookbook.

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.295
I love cookbooks.
-Oh, wow.

00:03:50.295 --> 00:03:52.865
-Yeah.
This one is called

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:57.803
"Cooking in the Nude
for Playful Gourmets."

00:03:57.803 --> 00:04:01.207
I think it's probably not a safe
idea, but what would I know?

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.775
Let's look at a recipe.

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.410
Cream cheese balls.

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:09.949
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.617
Cream cheese balls.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:14.153
-That seems pretty safe.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.855
-I don't even have to look
at the recipe.

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:16.989
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:19.191
-Go ahead, read it,
go ahead, go ahead.

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:21.427
-Been there. Smeared that.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.796
-Uh-oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.732
-Oh, cream cheese balls.

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:27.100
-Want to try it?

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:31.604
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.873
-Well, we're down
to our last book here.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:36.942
This is a children's book
called

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.277
"The Ha-Ha Powder."

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:43.816
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:45.985
Just a fun, upbeat book
about clowns

00:04:45.985 --> 00:04:48.387
that are into weird bags
of powder that make you happy.

00:04:48.387 --> 00:04:50.790
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.025
-Got to be the sequel.
-I'm sure it's safe for --

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:54.560
Look who makes the book.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:55.695
Look at that thing.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.462
Hey.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.462 --> 00:05:00.399
Happy birthday, kids.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:01.533
That's all I have
for this edition

00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:02.735
of my "Do Not Read" list.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.136
If you have a book that
you think should be

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:06.605
on our next "Do Not Read" list,
I'd love to see it.

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:09.709 line:0%
Send your titles to
donotread@tonightshow.com.

